inal report and recommendations, 2020. 55. Gerber L, González-Suárez M. Population viability analysis: Origins and contributions. Na Educ Knowledge 2010;3(10). 56. Gwinn M, MacCannell D, Armstrong GL. Next-Generation Sequencing of Infectious Pathogens. JAMA. 2019;321(9):893–4. 10.1001/jama.2018.21669. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] 57. Centers for Disease Control and Prevention . Framework for program evaluation in public health. Atlanta: US Department of Health and Human Services; 1999. [ Google Scholar ] 58. Calba C, Goutard FL, Hoinville L, Hendrikx P, Lindberg A, Saegerman C, Peyre M. Surveillance systems evaluation: a systematic review of the existing approaches. BMC Public Health. 2015;15(1):448. doi: 10.1186/s12889-015-1791-5. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] Associated Data This section collects any data citations, data availability statements, or supplementary materials included in this article. Supplementary Materials 13073_2021_934_MOESM1_ESM.docx (13.5KB, docx) Additional file 1. Literature review search terms and databases. 13073_2021_934_MOESM2_ESM.docx (17.9KB, docx) Additional file 2. Studies and reports included in the literature review. 13073_2021_934_MOESM3_ESM.docx (18.1KB, docx) Additional file 3. The evaluation framework: Key activities in utilising pathogen WGS in public health and associated outputs, outcomes and indicators. 13073_2021_934_MOESM4_ESM.docx (15.4KB, docx) Additional file 4: Table S1. Indicators and data collection methods. 13073_2021_934_MOESM5_ESM.docx (14.9KB, docx) Additional file 5: Table S2. Application of the evaluation framework for Listeria monocytogenes WGS. 13073_2021_934_MOESM6_ESM.docx (14.9KB, docx) Additional file 6: Table S3. Application of the evaluation framework for Mycobacterium tuberculosis WGS. 13073_2021_934_MOESM7_ESM.docx (14.9KB, docx) Additional file 7: Table S4. Application of the evaluation framework for SARS-CoV-2 WGS. Data Availability Statement Not applicable.',5