[ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 54. Jang H.D., Kim E.H., Lee J.C., Choi S.W., Kim K., Shin B.J. Current Concepts in the Management of Osteoporotic Vertebral Fractures: A Narrative Review. Asian Spine J. 2020;14:898–909. doi: 10.31616/asj.2020.0594. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 55. Bernetti A., Agostini F., Cacchio A., Santilli V., Ruiu P., Paolucci T., Paoloni M., Mangone M. Postural Evaluation in Sports and Sedentary Subjects by Rasterstereographic Back Shape Analysis. Appl. Sci. 2020;10:8838. doi: 10.3390/app10248838. [ DOI ] [ Google Scholar ] 56. Stanghelle B., Bentzen H., Giangregorio L., Pripp A.H., Skelton D.A., Bergland A. Physical fitness in older women with osteoporosis and vertebral fracture after a resistance and balance exercise programme: 3-month post-intervention follow-up of a randomised controlled trial. BMC Musculoskelet. Disord. 2020;21:471. doi: 10.1186/s12891-020-03495-9. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 57. Hoke M., Omar N.B., Amburgy J.W., Self D.M., Schnell A., Morgan S., Larios E.A., Chambers M.R. Impact of exercise on bone mineral density, fall prevention, and vertebral fragility fractures in postmenopausal osteoporotic women. J. Clin. Neurosci. 2020;76:261–263. doi: 10.1016/j.jocn.2020.04.040. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 58. Gibbs J.C., MacIntyre N.J., Ponzano M., Templeton J.A., Thabane L., Papaioannou A., Giangregorio L.M. Exercise for improving outcomes after osteoporotic vertebral fracture. Cochrane Database Syst. Rev. 2019;7:CD008618. doi: 10.1002/14651858.CD008618.pub3. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 59. Evidence Service to Support the COVID-19 Response. [(accessed on 1 January 2021)]; Available online: http://www.cebm.net/oxford-centre-evidence-based-medicine-levels-evidence-march-2009/ Associated Data This section collects any data citations, data availability statements, or supplementary materials included in th