ould C Vandervelde L Batcho CS, et al. : Can manual ability be measured with a generic ABILHAND scale? A cross-sectional study conducted on six diagnostic groups. BMJ Open 2012;2:e001807. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 26. Simone A Rota V Tesio L, et al. : Generic ABILHAND questionnaire can measure manual ability across a variety of motor impairments. Int J Rehabil Res 2011;34:131–40 [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 27. Miller GA: The magical number seven plus or minus two: some limits on our capacity for processing information. Psychol Rev 1956;63:81–97 [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 28. Ma WJ, Husain M, Bays PM: Changing concepts of working memory. Nat Neurosci 2014;17:347–56 [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 29. Franchignoni F, Salaffi F, Tesio L: How should we use the Visual Analogue Scale (VAS) in rehabilitation outcomes? I: how much of what? The seductive VAS numbers are not true measures. J Rehabil Med 2012;44:798–9 [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 30. Kelley TL: Interpretation of Educational Measurements . Yonkers-on-Hudson, NY, World Book Company, 1927 [ Google Scholar ] 31. Guilford JP: New standards for test evaluation. Educ Psychol Meas 1946;6:427–38 [ Google Scholar ] 32. Borsboom D, Mellenbergh GJ, Van Heerden J: The concept of validity. Psychol Rev 2004;111:1061–71 [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 33. Agazzi E: Scientific Objectivity and Its Contexts . Heidelberg, Springer International Publishing, 2014. doi: 10.1007/978-3-319-04660-0 [ DOI ] [ Google Scholar ] 34. Buzzoni M, Tesio L, Stuart MT: Holism and Reductionism in the Illness/Disease Debate, in Wuppuluri S, Stewart I (eds): From Electrons to Elephants and Elections. The Frontiers Collection . Cham, Springer, 2022:743–78 [ Google Scholar ] 35. Tesio L: Measurement in clinical vs. biological medicine: the Rasch model as a bridge on a widening gap. J Appl Meas 2004;5:362–6 [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ]',122,'2025-10-20 07:09:28','