y exploring the United Kingdom context. Health Res Policy Syst. 2016;14:23. doi: 10.1186/s12961-016-0093-4. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 21. Hanney S, Kuruvilla S, Soper B, Mays N. Who needs what from a national health research system: lessons from reforms to the English Department of Health''s R&D system. Health Res Policy Syst. 2010;8:11. doi: 10.1186/1478-4505-8-11. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 22. Hanney SR, González-Block MA. Organising health research systems as a key to improving health: the world health report 2013 and how to make further progress. Health Res Policy Syst. 2013;11:47. doi: 10.1186/1478-4505-11-47. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 23. Green G. Power to the people: to what extent has public involvement in applied health research achieved this? Res Involv Engagem. 2016;2:28. doi: 10.1186/s40900-016-0042-y. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 24. Dodgson R Lee K, Drager N. Global Health Governance: A Conceptual Review. Centre on Global Change and Health, London School of Hygiene & Tropical Medicine/World Health Organization. https://researchonline.lshtm.ac.uk/18031/1/a85727_eng.pdf . Accessed 24 Aug 2018. 25. Saltman RB, Ferroussier-Davis O. The concept of stewardship in health policy. Bull World Health Organ. 2000;78(6):732–739. [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 26. Pang T, Sadana R, Hanney S, Bhutta ZA, Hyder AA, Simon J. Knowledge for better health: a conceptual framework and foundation for health research systems. Bull World Health Organ. 2003;81(11):815–820. [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 27. Milewa T, Buxton M, Hanney S. Lay involvement in the public funding of medical research: expertise and counter-expertise in empirical and analytical perspective. Crit Public Health. 2008;18(3):357–366. doi: 10.1080/09581590802084838. [ DOI ] [ Google Scholar ] 28. INVOLVE. What is Public Involvement in Researc